1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
Fix the underlying set X: the metric space of the plane, R squared.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,000
Work inside the ambient coordinate plane.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,400
Pick a point x in X.

4
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,400
The epsilon-ball about x is every point y whose distance to x is less than epsilon.

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,900
The dashed rim marks an open boundary: distances are strictly less than epsilon.

6
00:00:11,866 --> 00:00:13,066
With the ball gadget in hand, we can define open sets.

